If these components do not exist yet, create them carefully in a reusable blog component file instead of duplicating large inline style objects across every post.

Do not refactor every existing blog post at once unless explicitly asked.

When creating reusable components:

* preserve the existing dark CamCashGrl editorial style
* keep mobile layouts clean
* use rounded cards
* use subtle borders
* use readable contrast
* use gradient CTA buttons
* avoid huge bloated spacing

## Metadata Pattern

Use this pattern for blog metadata:

```js
export const metadata = {
  title: POST_TITLE,
  description: POST_DESCRIPTION,
  alternates: { canonical: CANONICAL_URL },
  openGraph: {
    title: POST_TITLE,
    description: POST_DESCRIPTION,
    url: CANONICAL_URL,
    type: 'article',
    images: [{ url: 'https://www.camcashgrl.com/og-image.png', width: 1200, height: 630 }],
  },
  twitter: {
    card: 'summary_large_image',
    title: POST_TITLE,
    description: POST_DESCRIPTION,
  },
}
```

## Article Schema Pattern

Use this pattern for article schema:

```js
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: POST_TITLE,
  description: POST_DESCRIPTION,
  url: CANONICAL_URL,
  datePublished: DATE_PUBLISHED,
  dateModified: DATE_MODIFIED,
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'CamCash', url: 'https://www.camcashgrl.com' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'CamCash', url: 'https://www.camcashgrl.com' },
  mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': CANONICAL_URL },
}
```

## FAQ Schema Rules

If a post includes FAQ schema, the visible FAQ content must match the schema.

Use this pattern:

```js
{
  '@type': 'Question',
  name: QUESTION,
  acceptedAnswer: {
    '@type': 'Answer',
    text: ANSWER,
  },
}
```

